body:
So I'm trying to pass the `contain` key to a `$table->get()` call which results in a fatal error. Here is the set up I'm using:

``` php
// Manufacturers Table
class ManufacturersTable extends ProductsAppTable {

    public function initialize(array $config) {
        parent::initialize($config);
        $this->hasMany('Products.Products');
        $this->belongsToMany('Products.ProductTypes', [
            'through' => 'Products.Products'
        ]);
    }

}

// Products Model
class ProductsTable extends ProductsAppTable {

    public function initialize(array $config) {
        parent::initialize($config);
        $this->belongsTo('Products.Manufacturers');
        $this->belongsTo('Products.ProductTypes', [
            'propertyName' => 'type'
        ]);
    }

}

// Product Types Table
class ProductTypesTable extends ProductsAppTable {

    public function initialize(array $config) {
        parent::initialize($config);
        $this->hasMany('Products.Products');
        $this->belongsToMany('Products.Manufacturers', [
            'through' => 'Products.Products'
        ]);
    }

}

// Manufacturers Controller
class ManufacturersController extends ProductsAppController {

    public function products($id = null) {

        // Works as expected
        $manufacturer = $this->Manufacturers->get($id);
        debug($manufacturer);

        // Fatal Error
        $options = ['contain' => ['ProductTypes']];
        $manufacturer = $this->Manufacturers->get($id, $options);
        debug($manufacturer);

        // Fatal Error
        $association = $this->Manufacturers->association('ProductTypes');
        $target = $association->target();
        $foreignKey = $target->foreignKey();
        debug($foreignKey);

    }
}
```

The fatal error that I am getting is from `Cake\ORM\Association\BelongsToMany` on line [918](https://github.com/cakephp/cakephp/blob/3.0/src/ORM/Association/BelongsToMany.php#L918). It's trying to call `foreignKey()` on the target table and that method does not exist. In other parts of my application I have contained BTM data successfully so I believe this is probably something to do with the `through` key.

I thought this was something in my configuration but I haven't done anything out of the ordinary on this plugin and it still manages to call a method that does not exist. Running a `debug()` on that `$association` variable in the controller produces this:

